  "notes": "Original authored, unapproved six-second candidate. Begins in a stable two-palm hang to isolate the supported action. A stationary thin overhead platform represents the horizontal bar, not a ground obstacle. Two full controlled pendular cycles and a smaller final half-swing decay into a settled hang. Palms stay at (14,185) and (22,185) through frame 125. The head tips back to look toward the grip without arms drawing across its outline. Release precedes a short accelerating drop, both feet seat at frame 135, knees absorb the landing, and the locked stance recovers to neutral. Explicit world-space targets and null ground anchors prevent ground correction from moving loaded grips. No new prop renderer or gate exceptions. Platform color is requested but the existing platform renderer does not honor per-prop color.",
